Z||000000||Uaana||08-30-2000||11:32 PM||||Anyone here know who owns a White 88 Formula (in desperate need of a wash) in the TC area? I keep passing this guy on 394 at the 94 split eastbound around 5:30pm everyday. It could be a nice car, just doesnt look like he's keeping up with it. Just thinking to myself with my beat looking 87GT that I'd love to have an 88 in that clean of shape. It almost hurts to see someone neglect someting that could be so nice.||||reg||1
Z||000001||T1H2 0||08-31-2000||01:14 PM||||Wasn't me.  Mine isn't white, it's red.  It's alto a GT.  It makes me pretty mad when I see a crappy Fiero.  I know some people have ones that aren't the nicest, but at least they know the rarity of them and take care of them.  I bet that guy drives it in the winter too.  <P>------------------<BR>Quit lookin' at me like that.  I could waste you if I wanted to.  Just don't want to hurt my Fiero.||||reg||10
Z||000002||DjKid||08-31-2000||09:14 PM||||I drive my car during the winter, thats what its is, a car to be driven. Does that make me a bad person? I think not. <P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||8
Z||000003||Standard||08-31-2000||09:31 PM||||Both my Fiero's <B>look</B> pretty crappy, but I try to keep them mechanicly sound which is what matters most to me right now, as I don't have the money to make them run good <B>and</B> look good right now... I will also be driving my 84 through the winter because it happens to be a very fun winter car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">   <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000004||T1H2 0||09-02-2000||12:19 PM||||No, I wasn't saying that you are a bad person if you drive your Fiero in the winter.  I was saying that I don't like to see people treating their vehicles the way they do.  It doesn't matter if it doesn't look the best; mine certainly doesn't.  The thing that matters is that you take care of it.  I also am in the process of looking for a winter Fiero.  I have an old beater to use right now, and I want something that will be a little more reliable.  The beater is a rear-wheel drive.  Well, I know that Fieros are, but with the  engine placed in the rear, the traction has to be good.  It will handle ten times better than the other.  I don't care if it's the crappiest Fiero in the world, but I would take care of it, because I know how much work cars are and how much pleasure you can get from them.  That's what kind of good with being broke.  You can work for your Fiero to fix it, and then you will treat it well because you had to save and wait and save and wait.  When you are the "rich" folk, you just buy what is needed to fix it, and won't care because you didn't have to save and wait.  That's all I was saying.  Sorry if I made you upset at me, and now I know I have to phrase everything I say a little better.  Thanks.||||reg||1
